# Stage 9 back wall (factor 16: moves with the room; factor_y 0),
# opaque over the full 180 px (the sky is never drawn). Rows 0-19: the
# ceiling band, the stuck tile's look (cornice c/w/o/O). Cream c walls
# with fluted c/w/o pilasters (every 160 px) carrying pairs of w/i
# tulip sconces on o/O arms; a dark-green G/j wainscot (no light top
# lip) from y 108; two tall arched windows (w/i casing, n/R drapes
# with o ties, an O/l board as the sill) onto the Pfarrgasse: s/h sky,
# p/c facades with T windows, the queue as tiny figures on the i
# street, and through the first the Stadtpfarrkirche (c/o tower, t/T
# spire, as on the route map); a Y/o/O-framed mirror (h/i glass, w
# streaks, a pointed cartouche), two o/O-framed paintings (Y lit left) (the
# Katrin, the Traun). In front of the wainscot, smaller and muted:
# marble tables i/m on l/O pedestals with a Melange w, Thonet chairs
# l/O, guests reading newspapers i/w/m on o holders. No k, nothing
# with a light lip (D-038). The platform chandeliers' o chains hang
# at world x mod 640 = 8 (L1, row 11), 56, 168, 280, 584 (row 10)
# and end in a small O/l bowl under the luster band (y 68 / 84 on
# screen at camera y 92). The floor rows (148+) are hidden by marmor.
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grid is the source.
sprite = bg_zauner_salon
size   = 640x180
origin = 0,0
anim   = idle frames=1
---
frame idle 0




















































































































































































